to-daniel-gross-source : List Word
to-daniel-gross-source = lines-of (cons "# Daniel Gross"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Daniel, this page is for you, and it takes your own thesis about talent as its starting point. Each claim below about Avik Jain's work links to the block of his paper, *hyperactivity*, Part I, that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## The thesis you have been right about"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You told Tyler Cowen that in venture the costly mistake is missing great people, and that great talent always looks very weird to whatever convention is. Intellect is overvalued in founders; energy and persistence through repeated failure count for more. *Talent* (2022), the book you wrote with Cowen, turns these into a method. The professions that hire for a living mostly reason the other way: credentials, affiliation, legibility to committees."
  (cons ""
  (cons "You built institutions on the claim and let it be tested. You came to Y Combinator from Jerusalem as its youngest founder to date. Apple bought Cue in 2013, and in 2017 you became a YC partner and started its AI program. In August 2018 you founded Pioneer, a remote accelerator meant to find ambitious people anywhere. With Nat Friedman you ran AI Grant, co-founded NFDG, and, with Brent Seales, launched the Vesuvius Challenge on March 15, 2023. On February 5, 2024, its grand prize went to three students, Youssef Nader, Luke Farritor and Julian Schilliger, who read Greek text from PHerc. Paris. 4, sealed since 79 AD. A prize, open data and an open leaderboard found people no hiring process would have found. That is undervalued because it makes the gatekeepers unnecessary for the problems it suits."
  (cons ""
  (cons "In June 2024 you co-founded Safe Superintelligence with Ilya Sutskever and Daniel Levy, around the position that safety is part of the definition of superintelligence, not something added later. In July 2025 you moved to Meta Superintelligence Labs."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What this work is, on your terms"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Hyperactivity is one such person and idea. Avik Jain studied EECS at Berkeley and reached USACO Platinum. As an undergraduate he was first author of value-alignment work in Anca Dragan's lab. He turned down a Jane Street offer and an OpenAI offer, and then spent ten years outside academic publishing on a single product. By your criteria the signal is the energy, the persistence and the refusal of convention."
  (cons ""
  (cons "In Avik's words, the product is “a language and a computational model of reality i.e. wolfram's ruliad executing on silicon”. Its core is the CCHM cubical calculus with clock-indexed guarded computation"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ". The paper's subtitle names it a decentralized operating system language for collective superintelligence, and its sense is exact, reusable reasoning available through interactions, with established conclusions keeping the evidence and dependencies that govern their use"
  (cons (cite s1-3-p4 "(§1.3)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "This bears directly on what you set out to build at Safe Superintelligence. If safety is part of the definition, it has to be carried by construction. In the paper a requirement is a chosen dependent family, and the reasoning that establishes it is a term of the same language as the program"
  (cons (cite s1-p25 "(1.5)")
  (cons "; tests observe selected executions, whereas that term concerns every input in its stated domain"
  (cons (cite s1-p26 "(§1)")
  (cons ". An observation determines the fiber of histories compatible with it, and what it warrants is a construction over that whole fiber"
  (cons (cite s1-p12 "(1.3)")
  (cons "; refining the observation can only shrink the fiber, so a conclusion established on the coarser fiber stays established"
  (cons (cite s1-p13 "(§1)")
  (cons ". The same construction states when an action is safe: evidence over every compatible state, without guessing the hidden one"
  (cons (cite s1-p14 "(§1)")
  (cons ". Avik holds that intelligence at its end state is reasoning over equality and the paths between equalities."
  (cons ""
  (cons "It reaches further than its name suggests. One language covers content-addressed definitions exchanged with their proofs"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p7 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ", maintained results updated with their correctness evidence"
  (cons (cite s10-p9 "(§10)")
  (cons ", and specialization that returns a path to the program it specializes"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p6 "(§6.2)")
  (cons ". Avik adds, in his own words, that “the interaction system can model crypto primitives & hardness assumptions as well, it's really the endgame of the field”."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Why you, and what you receive"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik described the people he most wants to reach as “a class of humans oriented the opposite way without any deep expertise but deep receptivity to expertise”, and he named successful venture capitalists as that class. Experts deep in one field have a frame to defend; you have spent a career selecting for whatever does not fit the frame."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Everything here gives you full credit for the work of yours it builds on: the talent thesis, Pioneer, the Challenge's model of open problems with verifiable results, and the insistence that safety belongs in the definition of superintelligence. Read this looking for the best in it, and judge it as you judge talent, by what it does."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik is assembling one shared conversation among the people whose work this closes or serves: type theorists, cryptographers, distributed-systems researchers, Yejin Choi, Stuart Russell, and a small number of investors with your orientation. Your place in it is as the person who has thought hardest about how to find what convention misses."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Conversations with Tyler, Ep. 150, Daniel Gross and Tyler Talk Talent, https://conversationswithtyler.com/episodes/daniel-gross/"
  (cons "- Daniel Gross (businessman), Wikipedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Gross_(businessman)"
  (cons "- Vesuvius Challenge grand prize, https://scrollprize.org/grandprize"
  (cons "- SiliconANGLE, 3 July 2025, Safe Superintelligence CEO Daniel Gross joins Meta's new AI lab, https://siliconangle.com/2025/07/03/safe-superintelligence-ceo-daniel-gross-joins-metas-new-ai-lab/"
  (cons "- Talent, Tyler Cowen and Daniel Gross, Hachette, https://www.hachette.co.uk/titles/tyler-cowen/talent/9781529376432/"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Part I, the blocks linked above"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
